<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariconium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ariconium was a Romano-British town near Weston-under-Penyard, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ross-on-wye">Ross-on-Wye</a> in Herefordshire, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. It was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-working">iron-working</a> that used ore from the Forest of Dean, and it gave its name to the post-Roman Welsh kingdom of Ergyng, later the English district of Archenfield.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ariconium.jpg" alt="Ariconium" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pauline Eccles · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_over_Bury_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_906849.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
